C     RW SPAD FORTRAN MONITOR ROUTINE.   01 AUGUST, 1960.               SPAD0001
C     01 AUGUST, 1960  (DIMENSIONS ARE SETUP FOR A 32K MACHINE, AND     SPAD0002
C      THE ROUTINE IS PREPARED FOR THE 709 FORTRAN MONITOR SYSTEM.)     SPAD0003
C     TAPES A-4 (4), B-2 (10), AND B-6 (14) ARE USED ON THE VARIOUS     SPAD0004
C      OPTIONS. HOWEVER, THE USER MAY CHANGE THESE TAPE UNITS IN THE    SPAD0005
C      SETUP SUBROUTINE. (SEE NUT1, NUT2, NUT3, NINPT.)                 SPAD0006
C     GLOSSARY OF SYMBOLS FROM SPAD SUB. TO SPAD WRITEUP.               SPAD0007
C     SPAD SUB.   SPAD WRITEUP AND EXPLANATIONS OF SYMBOLS.             SPAD0008
C                                                                       SPAD0009
C     IOU(50)   = L1  NO. OF MESH UNITS IN X DIRECTION FROM Y AXIS.     SPAD0010
C                     FOR A RECTANGULAR (OR SQUARE) AREA L1 WILL BE 0.  SPAD0011
C                     FOR A CURVED AREA L1 WILL VARY WITH EACH ROW.     SPAD0012
C     KN(50)    = L2  NODE PT. NUMBER (NAME) CORRESPONDING TO PTS. OF L1SPAD0013
C     MAXI(50)  = L3  NO. OF REG. INT. PTS. IN ITH ROW. OF L1(I)        SPAD0014
C     NSTO(10000)=L4  LIST OF FIXED PT. PORTIONS OF POINT RECORDS(INPUT)SPAD0015
C     ASTO(9900) =C5  LIST OF FLOAT.PT. PORTIONS OF POINT RECORDS(INPUT)SPAD0016
C     JV(1)     = N2  ORDINATE VALUE OF LOWEST ROW IN UNITS OF K, IN    SPAD0017
C                     FIXED PT.  DISTANCE OF LOWEST ROW FROM X-AXIS.    SPAD0018
C     NUMBR(1)  = N1  NO. OF INPUT PT. RECORDS.  (SEE L4 AND C5).       SPAD0019
C     MAXJ(1)   = N3  TOTAL ROWS IN FIXED POINT.                        SPAD0020
C     OMEGA(1)  = OMG OVERRELAXATION FACTOR.  (BETWEEN 1. AND 2.)       SPAD0021
C     V (2000)  = UIJ SOLUTION VALUES.                                  SPAD0022
C     SH(1)     = DX  MESH SIZE IN X-DIRECTION.                         SPAD0023
C     SK(1)     = DY  MESH SIZE IN Y-DIRECTION.                         SPAD0024
C     NUPPP(1)  = N4  NO. OF NEIGHBORS IN PT. PATTERN. (TOTAL PTS.)     SPAD0025
C     MX(25)    = L6  PT. PATTERN NOS. OF X.  (EX. 1,0,-1,0)            SPAD0026
C     MWHY(25)  = L7  PT. PATTERN NOS. OF Y.  (EX. 0,1,0,-1)            SPAD0027
C     KDPV(1)   = N5  NO. OF DEPENDENT VARIABLES OR EQNS. (U AND W)     SPAD0028
C     INCD(1)   = N6  ALPHA (SEE SEVERAL DEPENDENT VAR. SECT. C)        SPAD0029
C                     ALPHA DIVIDES V STORAGE AMONG DEPENDENT VARIABLES.SPAD0030
C                     THUS, IF U REQUIRES 500 PTS., SET ALPHA=500       SPAD0031
C                     ASSUMING N5=2 (2 DEPENDENT VAR.)  ALSO, INCREASE  SPAD0032
C                     DIMENSION OF V IF NECESSARY.                      SPAD0033
C     NPAIR(1)  = N7  NO. OF ITEMS IN LIST L8 . (NO. OF L8=L9)          SPAD0034
C     KOMIT(50) = L8  LIST OF PTS. TO BE OMITTED. LEFT PT. (STARTING)   SPAD0035
C     LOMIT(50) = L9  LIST OF PTS. TO BE OMITTED.  RIGHT PT. (ENDING)   SPAD0036
C     NA4(1)    = N8  NO. OF ITEMS IN L4.  (TOTAL CELLS)                SPAD0037
C     N111(1)   = N11 FLAG FOR NON-LINEAR PROBLEMS.  (0=LINEAR)         SPAD0038
C                  FOR NON-LINEAR PROBLEMS SPAD RETURNS TO STATEMENT    SPAD0039
C                  666, AND THE USER MUST ALLOW FOR THIS IN BOTH SETUP  SPAD0040
C                  AND COCAL. (SEE COMMENTS AFTER STATEMENT 125.)       SPAD0041
C                  N11 IS ALSO USED AS A TEST FOR THE END OF A CASE.    SPAD0042
C                  SET N11=-1 (NOT -0, SINCE FORTRAN TREATS -0 AS 0     SPAD0043
C                  IN AN IF TEST) IN THE CNVRG SUB IF ALL POINTS HAVE   SPAD0044
C                  CONVERGED.  SPAD WILL RETURN TO INSTRUCTION 1 FOR    SPAD0045
C                  THE NEXT CASE (AFTER SAVING THE U(I) ON TAPE NUT3 IF SPAD0046
C                  SAVE IS SET TO -1 IN SUB CNVRG, OR IF SS5 IS DOWN)   SPAD0047
C     EPS       = EPS EPSILON IS THE ACCURACY DESIRED FOR CONVERGENCE.  SPAD0048
C                     SPAD SETS EPS TO .0001.    EPS CAN BE CHANGED IN  SPAD0049
C                     THE SETUP SUBROUTINE IF DESIRED.                  SPAD0050
C     JWX1      =JWX1 FLAG WHICH IF MINUS, ALLOWS SPAD TO TEST FOR      SPAD0051
C                     CONVERGENCE.  IF JWX1=-, SPAD WILL KEEP ITERATING SPAD0052
C                     UNTIL ALL U(I) HAVE CONVERGED TO EPS DEC. PLACES. SPAD0053
C                     AFTER CONVERGENCE SPAD TRANSFERS TO THE CNVRG SUB.SPAD0054
C                     WHICH SHOULD BE USED FOR OUTPUT ONLY.  IF JWX1=+, SPAD0055
C                     THE USER MUST TEST FOR CONVERGENCE IN THE CNVRG   SPAD0056
C                     SUB.  SPAD TRANSFERS TO CNVRG AFTER EACH ITERATIONSPAD0057
C                     IF JWX1 IS PLUS.  (ALSO, SEE MX1)                 SPAD0058
C     JWX2      =JWX2 FLAG TO ALLOW SPAD TO USE TAPE OPERATIONS.        SPAD0059
C                  IF JWX2=-, TAPES NUT1 AND NUT2 WILL NOT BE USED.     SPAD0060
C                     IF JWX2=+K, SPAD WILL STORE ALL POINT RECORDS     SPAD0061
C                     ON TAPES NUT1 AND NUT2 IN GROUPS OF LPT PT.RECORDSSPAD0062
C                      LOADED PT. RECORDS (IF ANY) ARE PUT ON 1ST AS    SPAD0063
C                      1 GROUP.  THEN REG.INT.PT. RECORDS ARE WRITTEN   SPAD0064
C                      IN GROUPS OF LPT (LK TOTAL GROUPS) PT RECORDS.   SPAD0065
C                      THE DATA IS SAVED IN DUPLICATE ON TAPES NUT1     SPAD0066
C                      AND NUT2. THEN IN THE ITERATION FOR U(N) THE     SPAD0067
C                      LOADED PT. RECORDS ARE READ IN AND SOLVED.       SPAD0068
C                      THEREAFTER, REG.INT.PT. RECORDS ARE READ IN      SPAD0069
C                      GROUPS OF LPT PT. RECORDS AND SOLVED. THE TWO    SPAD0070
C                      TAPES ARE ALTERNATED AFTER EACH MAJOR ITERATION  SPAD0071
C                      TO SAVE REWIND TIME. JWX2 MUST BE LESS THAN THE  SPAD0072
C                      DIMENSION OF L4 BY AT LEAST 2(2+NUPPP*KDPV).     SPAD0073
C                      JWX2=+K SHOULD ONLY BE USED WHEN C.S. IS LIMITED.SPAD0074
C     SSW3      =SSW3 IF SENSE SWITCH SWITCH 3 IS DOWN, SPAD WILL TRA   SPAD0075
C                      TO CNVRG AFTER EACH MAJOR ITERATION.             SPAD0076
C     NINPT     =NINPT  IF NINPT=+, SPAD WILL READ U(N) FROM TAPE       SPAD0077
C                    NINPT.  NINPT IS REWOUND AFTER READING THE U(N).   SPAD0078
C     SAVE      =SAVE IF BOTH N111 AND SAVE ARE SET TO -1 IN SUB CNVRG, SPAD0079
C                  SPAD WILL SAVE THE FINAL U(N) ON TAPE NUT3.          SPAD0080
C     SSW5      =SSW5 IF SENSE SWITCH 5 IS DOWN, SPAD WILL SAVE THE     SPAD0081
C                    FINAL U(N) (2000 WORDS) ON TAPE NUT3 -- IF N111    SPAD0082
C                      IS SET TO MINUS IN THE CNVRG SUBROUTINE.  NOTE   SPAD0083
C                      THAT NUT3=NINPT.  THUS, THE INPUT DATA, IF ANY,  SPAD0084
C                      WILL BE DESTROYED. (CAN BE CHANGED IN SETUP.)    SPAD0085
C     MX1       = MX1 SPADE WILL TRANSFER TO CNVRG AFTER MX1 ITERATIONS SPAD0086
C                     EVEN THOUGH ALL THE U(I)  HAVE NOT CONVERGED.     SPAD0087
C                     (NPR WILL BE ZERO IF ALL U(I)  HAVE CONVERGED.)   SPAD0088
C                     THIS SHOULD BE USED WHERE SENSE SWITCHES ARE      SPAD0089
C                     NOT ALLOWED, AND WHEN JWX1 IS NEGATIVE.           SPAD0090
C                                                                       SPAD0091
C     SPAD SUB.   COCAL SUBROUTINE (SPAD WRITEUP)                       SPAD0092
C     SI(1)     = X   COORDINATE IN TERMS OF H (DX).                    SPAD0093
C     SJ(1)     = Y   COORDINATE IN TERMS OF K (DY).                    SPAD0094
C     AA(50)    = A   LIST OF COEFFICIENTS IN ORDER OF NUMBERS IN       SPAD0095
C                     POINT PATTERN.  (ALSO, SEE SEVERAL DEPENDENT VAR.)SPAD0096
C     INDX4     = N10 INTEGER ASSOCIATED WITH THE DEPENDENT VARIABLE.   SPAD0097
C                     INDX4 INDICATES WHICH OF THE EQNS. COEFFICIENTS   SPAD0098
C                     MUST BE GENERATED FOR. THUS, USER MUST BRANCH ON  SPAD0099
C                     INDX4 (IN COCAL) IF MORE THAN 1 DEPENDENT VARIABLESPAD0100
C     V(2000)   = U   FUNCTION VALUES AT MESH POINTS. U(I) = FUNCTION   SPAD0101
C                     VALUE AT NET POINT I. THERE WILL BE FUNCT. VALUES SPAD0102
C                     FOR ALL POINT RECORDS--THIS INCLUDES THE POINT    SPAD0103
C                     RECORDS WHICH MAY HAVE BEEN LOADED BY THE USER    SPAD0104
C                     AND THE POINT RECORDS FOR REG. INT. PTS GENERATED SPAD0105
C                     BY SPAD. ALL OF THE FORMER ARE SOLVED BEFORE THE  SPAD0106
C                     LATTER IN THE ITERATION SCHEME.                   SPAD0107
C     NSTO(L)   = N   MESH POINT NUMBER (NAME) CORRESPONDING TO MESH    SPAD0108
C                     POINT X AND Y.                                    SPAD0109
      DIMENSION LAZ(200), AA(50)                                        SPAD0110
C     THE DIMENSION OF LAZ IS THE MAXIMUM NUMBER OF POINTS WHICH CAN BE SPAD0111
C       OMITTED.  (SEE COMMENTS ABOVE STATEMENT 133 AND 134.)           SPAD0112
     0DIMENSION IOU(50),KN(50),MAXI(50),NSTO(10000),ASTO(9900),         SPAD0113
     1 V(2000),MX(25),MWHY(25),KOMIT(50),LOMIT(50)                      SPAD0114
C          PROGRAM BEGINS HERE.  (1ST STATEMENT OF SPAD)                SPAD0115
 1    EPS=.0001                                                         SPAD0116
      SAVE=+1.                                                          SPAD0117
      NUT1 = 4                                                          SPAD0118
      NUT2 = 10                                                         SPAD0119
      NINPT = -14                                                       SPAD0120
      NUT3  = XABSF(NINPT)                                              SPAD0121
C     NUT1, NUT2, NUT3, AND NINPT ARE TAPE UNITS USED IN SPADE (OPT.).  SPAD0122
C      IF USED, THEY MAY BE CHANGED TO OTHER UNITS BY THE USER IN       SPAD0123
C      THE SETUP SUBROUTINE.                                            SPAD0124
      LNSTO =  10000                                                    SPAD0125
      LASTO = 9900                                                      SPAD0126
                                                                        SPAD0127
      KUN   =   2000                                                    SPAD0128
C     KUN SHOULD EQUAL THE DIMENSION OF V.                              SPAD0129
      MX1   =   50                                                      SPAD0130
 66   JWX1=-1                                                           SPAD0131
      JWX2 = -9700                                                      SPAD0132
      I3=0                                                              SPAD0133
C                                                                       SPAD0134
 666  CALL SETUP (IOU,KN,MAXI,NSTO,ASTO,NUMBR,JV,MAXJ,OMEGA,            SPAD0135
     1   V,SH,SK,NUPPP,MX,MWHY,KDPV,INCD,NPAIR,KOMIT,LOMIT,NA4,N111,    SPAD0136
     2 EPS, JWX1, JWX2, I3, NUT1, NUT2, NUT3, NINPT, X1, X2, MX1, MX2)  SPAD0137
C     X1, X2, AND MX2 ARE NOT USED AT PRESENT.                          SPAD0138
      MMX1  =   MX1                                                     SPAD0139
      IF (NINPT) 661,661, 65                                            SPAD0140
 65   REWIND  NINPT                                                     SPAD0141
 661  IF (JWX2) 68,68, 67                                               SPAD0142
 67   REWIND  NUT1                                                      SPAD0143
      REWIND  NUT2                                                      SPAD0144
      JWX2A = LASTO - (LNSTO -JWX2)                                     SPAD0145
 68   SSJ = JV                                                          SPAD0146
C     SET SSJ TO ORDINATE VALUE OF LOWEST ROW.                          SPAD0147
      LPOR = NUPPP*KDPV                                                 SPAD0148
      LPOR1 = LPOR +1                                                   SPAD0149
      LPOR2 = LPOR +2                                                   SPAD0150
C                                                                       SPAD0151
C     GENERATE POINT RECORDS FOR INTERIOR PT.S                          SPAD0152
      NYC=0                                                             SPAD0153
C                                                                       SPAD0154
C     DO 134 FORMS A TABLE CONTAINING A LIST OF ALL OMITTED PTS.        SPAD0155
C     THUS, L8 AND L9 ARE SIMPLY EXPANDED TO ANOTHER TABLE (LAZ(LSST)). SPAD0156
C     NPAIR (N7) IS THE NO. OF ITEMS IN LIST L8 (OR L9).                SPAD0157
C     L8 AND L9 CONTAIN A LIST OF PTS. TO BE OMITTED.  L8 CONTAINS      SPAD0158
C     THE STARTING PTS. WHILE L9 CONTAINS THE CORRESPONDING ENDING PTS. SPAD0159
C     DO 133 IS A MINOR LOOP WHICH EXPANDS EACH SET OF L8 AND L9.       SPAD0160
C     NYC IS THE LENGTH OF TABLE LAZ.  (TOTAL PTS. TO BE OMITTED).      SPAD0161
C                                                                       SPAD0162
      DO134JDEX=1,NPAIR                                                 SPAD0163
      LSPKT=LOMIT(JDEX)-KOMIT(JDEX)+1                                   SPAD0164
      DO133IDEX=1,LSPKT                                                 SPAD0165
      LSST=NYC+IDEX                                                     SPAD0166
 133  LAZ(LSST)=KOMIT(JDEX)+IDEX-1                                      SPAD0167
 134  NYC=NYC+LSPKT                                                     SPAD0168
C                                                                       SPAD0169
C     NA4 (N8) IS THE NO. OF CELLS OCCUPIED BY LIST L4,                 SPAD0170
C      WHERE L4 IS THE FIXED POINT PORTIONS OF THE POINT RECORDS        SPAD0171
C     L--L4(L) IS THE FIRST CELL FOLLOWING THE INPUT FIXED POINT        SPAD0172
C      PORTIONS OF POINT RECORDS                                        SPAD0173
C     NA5 IS THE NUMBER OF CELLS IN LIST C5, WHICH CONTAINS THE         SPAD0174
C      FLOATING POINT PORTIONS OF POINT RECORDS.  (EACH FLOATING POINT  SPAD0175
C      PORTION OF A RECORD OCCUPIES 1 LESS CELL THAN THE FIXED POINT    SPAD0176
C      PORTION OF THAT RECORD.)                                         SPAD0177
C     LL--C5(LL) IS THE FIRST CELL FOLLOWING THE INPUT FLOATING POINT   SPAD0178
C      PORTIONS                                                         SPAD0179
C                                                                       SPAD0180
      NA5=NA4-NUMBR                                                     SPAD0181
      IF(JWX2)72,72,70                                                  SPAD0182
 70   IF(NA4)72,72,71                                                   SPAD0183
 71   WRITE TAPE  NUT1, (NSTO(I), I =1, NA4), (ASTO(I), I = 1, NA5)     SPAD0184
      WRITE TAPE  NUT2, (NSTO(I), I =1, NA4), (ASTO(I), I = 1, NA5)     SPAD0185
      L=1                                                               SPAD0186
      LL=1                                                              SPAD0187
      GO TO 73                                                          SPAD0188
 72   L=NA4+1                                                           SPAD0189
       LL=NA5+1                                                         SPAD0190
 73   MAXYP=0                                                           SPAD0191
C                                                                       SPAD0192
C     DO 100 SEARCHES THE POINT PATTERN FOR THE ALGEBRAIC MAXIMUM AND   SPAD0193
C      MINIMUM Y-DISTANCES (MAXYP AND MINYP) FROM THE CENTER OF         SPAD0194
C      THE POINT PATTERN                                                SPAD0195
C     MAXYP--THE MAX. Y DISTANCE OF PT. PATTERN  (OF NEIGHBOR PTS.)     SPAD0196
C     NA6 IS THE NUMBER OF THE LAST ROW THAT MAY CONTAIN REGULAR        SPAD0197
C      INTERIOR PTS.                                                    SPAD0198
C                                                                       SPAD0199
      DO 100INDX1=1,NUPPP                                               SPAD0200
      MINYP= XMIN0F(MWHY(INDX1),MINYP)                                  SPAD0201
 100  MAXYP=XMAX0F(MWHY(INDX1),MAXYP)                                   SPAD0202
       MINYP=-MINYP                                                     SPAD0203
      NA6=MAXJ-MAXYP-1                                                  SPAD0204
C                                                                       SPAD0205
C     THIS SECTION GENERATES THE POINT RECORDS OF THE REGULAR INTERIOR  SPAD0206
C      POINTS, PROCEEDING IN ORDER OF INCREASING ROW NUMBER, AND        SPAD0207
C      FROM LEFT TO RIGHT WITHIN EACH ROW.                              SPAD0208
C     INDEX J COUNTS ON ROW NUMBER. (J+1 IS 1ST ROW WITH REG. INT. PTS.)SPAD0209
C     MIKKY--THE NUMBER OF MESH UNITS FROM THE Y-AXIS TO THE            SPAD0210
C      FIRST REGULAR INTERIOR POINT                                     SPAD0211
C                                                                       SPAD0212
 1010 LK=0                                                              SPAD0213
      LPT=0                                                             SPAD0214
      LPTA=0                                                            SPAD0215
      DO 171J=MINYP,NA6                                                 SPAD0216
      MIKKY=0                                                           SPAD0217
      NA7=MAXI(J+1)                                                     SPAD0218
      IF (NA7) 171,171,101                                              SPAD0219
C     JUMP TO 171 IF THERE ARE NO REGULAR INT. PTS. IN THE CURRENT ROW. SPAD0220
 101  MIKKY=MIKKY+1                                                     SPAD0221
C                                                                       SPAD0222
C     THIS LOOP SEARCHES THE ROW BEING PROCESSED (BEGINNING AT THE LEFT SPAD0223
C      END) FOR INTERIOR POINTS THAT ARE NOT REGULAR I.P.,              SPAD0224
C      UNTIL A REGULAR INTERIOR POINT IS ENCOUNTERED.                   SPAD0225
C     INDX1 COUNTS POSITION IN THE SET OF POINT PATTERN NUMBERS.        SPAD0226
C     INDX7 IS NUMBER OF ROW ON WHICH THE CURRENT POINT (OF POINT       SPAD0227
C      PATTERN) LIES                                                    SPAD0228
C     MIKKY IS INCREASED BY ONE IF ONE OF POINTS ADJACENT TO CURRENT PT.SPAD0229
C      IS AN EXTERIOR POINT (OUTSIDE THE BOUNDARY CURVE)                SPAD0230
C                                                                       SPAD0231
      DO 102INDX1=1,NUPPP                                               SPAD0232
      INDX7=J+MWHY(INDX1)+1                                             SPAD0233
      IF (IOU(INDX7)-MX(INDX1)-MIKKY)102,102,101                        SPAD0234
 102  CONTINUE                                                          SPAD0235
C                                                                       SPAD0236
C     NA7--L3(J+1), NUMBER OF REGULAR INTERIOR POINTS IN ROW            SPAD0237
C      BEING PROCESSED                                                  SPAD0238
C     NA777 IS THE NUMBER OF REGULAR INTERIOR POINTS, RELATIVE TO MIKKY.SPAD0239
C                                                                       SPAD0240
      IMS=KN(J+1)-IOU(J+1)                                              SPAD0241
      NA777=NA7+MIKKY-1                                                 SPAD0242
      SSSJ=J                                                            SPAD0243
      SJ=SSJ+SSSJ                                                       SPAD0244
C                                                                       SPAD0245
C     THIS LOOP GENERATES POINT RECORDS FOR REGULAR INTERIOR POINTS     SPAD0246
C      IN THE CURRENT ROW.                                              SPAD0247
C     SI IS FLOATING POINT VALUE (FOR COCAL) OF X-COORDINATE OF CURRENT SPAD0248
C      POINT (OF THE CURRENT ROW) (IN UNITS OF H)                       SPAD0249
C     SJ IS FLOATING POINT VALUE (FOR COCAL) OF Y-COORDINATE OF CURRENT SPAD0250
C      ROW (IN UNITS OF K) -- SSJ = N2 IN FLOATING POINT.               SPAD0251
C     NSTO(L) WILL CONTAIN THE NAME OF THE CURRENT REG. INT. PT. OF THE SPAD0252
C      CURRENT ROW.                                                     SPAD0253
C     KN(J+1) IS NAME OF FIRST INTERIOR OR BOUNDARY POINT IN CURRENT ROWSPAD0254
C     I IS COUNTER WHICH IS USED TO NAME SUCCESSIVE REGULAR INTERIOR PTSSPAD0255
C     THE LAST TERM ADDS A CONSTANT (AN INTEGRAL MULTIPLE OF ALPHA)     SPAD0256
C      TO DISTINGUISH NAMES OF POINTS OF SEVERAL DEPENDENT VARIABLES.   SPAD0257
C                                                                       SPAD0258
      DO 17INDX4=1,KDPV                                                 SPAD0259
      ICD = (INDX4 -1)*INCD                                             SPAD0260
      DO 17I=MIKKY,NA777                                                SPAD0261
 16   SI=I                                                              SPAD0262
      IMT = IMS +I                                                      SPAD0263
      NSTO(L) = IMT +ICD                                                SPAD0264
      DO135JDEX=1,NYC                                                   SPAD0265
      IF (IMT -LAZ(JDEX)) 135, 17, 135                                  SPAD0266
C                                                                       SPAD0267
C     TEST WHETHER CURRENT PT. IS IN LIST OF OMITTED PTS.               SPAD0268
C      IF YES, BYPASS COCAL (FOR THIS POINT).                           SPAD0269
 135  CONTINUE                                                          SPAD0270
C                                                                       SPAD0271
C     COCAL GENERATES THE COEFFICIENTS OF THE DIFFERENCE EQUATIONS,     SPAD0272
C      GIVEN X AND Y COORDINATES OF A REG. INT. PT. (USER MUST PROVIDE  SPAD0273
C      COCAL). INDX4 INDICATES WHICH OF THE EQUATIONS COEFFICIENTS ARE  SPAD0274
C      TO BE GENERATED FOR.  THUS, USER MUST BRANCH ON INDX4 IN COCAL,  SPAD0275
C      IF MORE THAN 1 EQUATION (SEE SEVERAL DEPENDENT VARIABLES).       SPAD0276
C     NSTO(L+1) CONTAINS THE TOTAL NO. OF COEFFICIENTS OF THE DIFFERENCESPAD0277
C      EQUATION FOR U(N). THE PROGRAM ASSUMES THAT THE VALUE OF EACH    SPAD0278
C      DEPENDENT VARIABLE AT EACH POINT OF THE POINT PATTERN ENTERS INTOSPAD0279
C      THE EQUATION. FOR EXAMPLE, IN A 4 PT. PATTERN AND 2 DEPENDENT    SPAD0280
C      VARIABLES, THE PROGRAM WILL ALLOW 8 STORAGES FOR THE COEFFICIENTSSPAD0281
C      EVEN IF THE LATTER FOUR ARE ZERO, AND THE CONSTANT TERM MUST BE  SPAD0282
C      STORED IN THE 9TH CELL (BY COCAL).                               SPAD0283
C                                                                       SPAD0284
      CALL COCAL(SI, SJ, AA, INDX4, V, NSTO(L), INCD,N111,SH,SK,X1,X2,  SPAD0285
     1 MX1, MX2)                                                        SPAD0286
C     X1, X2, AND MX2 ARE NOT USED AT PRESENT.                          SPAD0287
      NSTO(L+1) = LPOR                                                  SPAD0288
C                                                                       SPAD0289
C     THIS SECTION OF PROGRAM STORES THE POINT RECORD FOR THE CURRENT   SPAD0290
C      REGULAR INTERIOR POINT IN THE TABLES WHICH CONTAIN ALL THE POINT SPAD0291
C      RECORDS.  ONE EXECUTION OF THE LOOP STORES THE NAME OF A NEIGHBORSPAD0292
C      POINT N(I) IN TABLE L4, AND THE COEFFICIENT C(N(I)) IN TABLE C5. SPAD0293
C     IX CONTROLS REPETITION FOR EACH OF NEIGHBOR POINTS IN PT. PATTERN.SPAD0294
C     INDX5 CONTROLS REPETITION FOR EACH OF THE DEPENDENT VARIABLES.    SPAD0295
C     ITRM21--LOCATION OF THE COEFFICIENT C(N(I)) IN TABLE (SEE AA)     SPAD0296
C      OF COEFFICIENTS GENERATED BY COCAL                               SPAD0297
C     ITRM22--LOCATION AT WHICH N(I) IS TO BE STORED (CONSECUTIVELY)    SPAD0298
C     L--INITIAL LOCATION OF N(I) STORAGE                               SPAD0299
C     ITRM24--LOCATION AT WHICH C(N(I)) IS TO BE STORED (CONSECUTIVELY) SPAD0300
C     LL--INITIAL LOCATION OF THE C(N(I)) STORAGE                       SPAD0301
C     ITRM23--NUMBER OF ROW ON WHICH POINT N(I) IS LOCATED              SPAD0302
C     NSTO(ITRM22) CONTAINS THE NAME N(I) OF A NEIGHBOR POINT (USED IN  SPAD0303
C      CALCULATION OF U(N).)                                            SPAD0304
C     KN(ITRM23)=L2 (NODE PT. NAME) OF ROW ON WHICH N(I) IS LOCATED.    SPAD0305
C     I--NUMBER OF INTERIOR PTS. PREVIOUS TO FIRST REGULAR INTERIOR PT. SPAD0306
C     IOU(ITRM23)=L1 (NO. OF MESH UNITS IN X-DIRECTION FROM Y-AXIS) OF  SPAD0307
C      ROW ON WHICH POINT N(I) IS LOCATED.                              SPAD0308
C     LAST TERM ADDS MULTIPLE OF ALPHA IF SEVERAL DEPENDENT VARIABLES   SPAD0309
C     ASTO CONTAINS COEFFICIENT C(N(I))                                 SPAD0310
C                                                                       SPAD0311
      LP1 = L +1                                                        SPAD0312
      DO 103 IX = 1, NUPPP                                              SPAD0313
      ITRM23 = J +1 +MWHY(IX)                                           SPAD0314
      IMSV = KN(ITRM23) -IOU(ITRM23) +MX(IX)                            SPAD0315
      DO 103 INDX5 = 1, KDPV                                            SPAD0316
      ITRM21 = IX +(INDX5 -1)*NUPPP                                     SPAD0317
      ITRM22 = ITRM21 +LP1                                              SPAD0318
 103  NSTO(ITRM22) = IMSV +I +(INDX5 -1)*INCD                           SPAD0319
      L = L +LPOR2                                                      SPAD0320
      IEND = LL +LPOR                                                   SPAD0321
      JT = 1                                                            SPAD0322
      DO 105 IT=   LL, IEND                                             SPAD0323
      ASTO(IT)= AA(JT)                                                  SPAD0324
 105  JT = JT +1                                                        SPAD0325
      LL = IEND +1                                                      SPAD0326
C     INCREASE LL BY NO. OF CELLS OCCUPIED BY FLOATING POINT PORTION.   SPAD0327
      IF(JWX2)17,17,204                                                 SPAD0328
 204  LPT=LPT+1                                                         SPAD0329
C     LPT(=LPTA) IS THE NO. OF REG. INTERIOR PTS. IN A GROUP.           SPAD0330
C     JWX2 MUST BE SMALLER THAN THE DIMENSION OF L4 BY 2(2+NUPPP*KDPV). SPAD0331
      IF (L -JWX2) 208, 205,205                                         SPAD0332
 208  IF (LL -JWX2A) 17, 205, 205                                       SPAD0333
 205  WRITE TAPE  NUT1, (NSTO(M), M =1, L), (ASTO(M), M = 1, LL)        SPAD0334
      WRITE TAPE NUT2, (NSTO(M), M =1, L), (ASTO(M), M = 1, LL)         SPAD0335
      IF(LPTA-LPT)98,98,99                                              SPAD0336
 98   LPTA=LPT                                                          SPAD0337
C     LPTA WILL CONTAIN THE MAX. NO. OF REG. INT. PT. RECORDS           SPAD0338
C      IN A GROUP.  (FINAL GROUP MAY CONTAIN LESS.)                     SPAD0339
 99   LT=L                                                              SPAD0340
      LLT=LL                                                            SPAD0341
      L=1                                                               SPAD0342
      LL=1                                                              SPAD0343
      LK=LK+1                                                           SPAD0344
      LPT=0                                                             SPAD0345
C     LK (=LKA) IS THE NO. OF GROUPS OF REG. INTERIOR POINT             SPAD0346
C      RECORDS SAVED ON TAPES NUT1 (8) AND NUT2 (9).                    SPAD0347
 17   CONTINUE                                                          SPAD0348
 171  CONTINUE                                                          SPAD0349
      IF (JWX2) 19,19, 42                                               SPAD0350
 42   IF (LPT) 18,18, 41                                                SPAD0351
 41   WRITE TAPE  NUT1, (NSTO(M), M = 1, LT), (ASTO(M), M = 1, LLT)     SPAD0352
      WRITE TAPE  NUT2, (NSTO(M), M = 1, LT), (ASTO(M), M = 1, LLT)     SPAD0353
      LK=LK+1                                                           SPAD0354
 18   REWIND  NUT1                                                      SPAD0355
      REWIND  NUT2                                                      SPAD0356
 19   IF (NINPT) 207,207, 206                                           SPAD0357
 206  READ TAPE  NINPT, (V(I), I = 1, KUN)                              SPAD0358
C     KUN SHOULD EQUAL THE DIMENSION OF V.  (OR U)                      SPAD0359
      REWIND  NINPT                                                     SPAD0360
C     READ GUESSES FROM PREVIOUS RUN.  (IF NINPT=+)                     SPAD0361
 207  NA32 = 0                                                          SPAD0362
      LQ=MAXJ-MAXYP-1                                                   SPAD0363
C                                                                       SPAD0364
C     DO 27 COMPUTES NA32, THE TOTAL NUMBER OF REGULAR INTERIOR POINTS. SPAD0365
C     MINYP AND LQ ARE RESPECTIVELY THE FIRST AND LAST ROWS             SPAD0366
C      IN WHICH THERE MAY BE REGULAR INTERIOR POINTS.                   SPAD0367
C                                                                       SPAD0368
C     NPONT IS THE TOTAL NUMBER OF POINT RECORDS. ((NA32-NYC) IS THE    SPAD0369
C      NO. OF POINT RECORDS FOR REGULAR INTERIOR PTS.)  NYC IS THE TOTALSPAD0370
C      (IF ANY) NO. OF POINTS TO BE OMITTED.                            SPAD0371
C                                                                       SPAD0372
      DO 27J=MINYP,LQ                                                   SPAD0373
 27   NA32=NA32+MAXI(J+1)                                               SPAD0374
      IF(NPAIR)137,136,137                                              SPAD0375
C     IF THERE ARE NO OMITTED POINTS, NYC (INITIALLY 1) MUST BE SET TO 0SPAD0376
 136  NYC=0                                                             SPAD0377
 137  NPONT = (NA32 -NYC)*KDPV +NUMBR                                   SPAD0378
C                                                                       SPAD0379
C        HERE BEGINS THE ITERATION SECTION OF THE PROGRAM.              SPAD0380
C        THE POINT RECORDS SUPPLIED BY THE PROGRAMMER OR GENERATED      SPAD0381
C         BY COCAL CONTAIN ALL INFORMATION                              SPAD0382
C                                                                       SPAD0383
C                                                                       SPAD0384
C        NPR   --IF SPAD CHECKS CONVERGENCE DURING AN ITERATION,        SPAD0385
C         NPR COUNTS THE NUMBER OF V(I) THAT HAVE CONVERGED.            SPAD0386
C        NKONT --THE NUMBER OF V(I) ALREADY COMPUTED DURING             SPAD0387
C         AN ITERATION.                                                 SPAD0388
C        LIMIT --THE NUMBER OF V(I) COMPUTED FROM THE BEGINNING         SPAD0389
C         OF AN ITERATION TO THE END OF THE GROUP PRESENTLY IN          SPAD0390
C         CORE.  (NORMAL CASE, ALL RECORDS IN CORE, LIMIT               SPAD0391
C         INITIALIZED TO NPONT.)                                        SPAD0392
C        LA   --ADDRESS OF 2ND ENTRY IN THE FIXED-POINT RECORD          SPAD0393
C         OF THE NEXT V(I), THE NUMBER OF NEIGHBOR PTS. IN ITS          SPAD0394
C         RECORD.                                                       SPAD0395
C        IHK   --THE NUMBER OF V(I), OF THE GROUP PRESENTLY IN          SPAD0396
C         CORE, ALREADY COMPUTED, +2.                                   SPAD0397
C                                                                       SPAD0398
 138  NPR = NPONT                                                       SPAD0399
      NKONT = 0                                                         SPAD0400
      LIMIT = NPONT                                                     SPAD0401
      LA = 2                                                            SPAD0402
      IHK = 2                                                           SPAD0403
      OMEGB = OMEGA -1.                                                 SPAD0404
C                                                                       SPAD0405
C        INITIALIZE SWITCH  NTP  TO NORMAL CASE--INPUT POINT            SPAD0406
C         RECORDS PRECEDE RECORDS OF REGULAR INTERIOR POINTS.           SPAD0407
C        INITIALIZE SWITCH  IESKP  TO NORMAL CASE--ALL POINT            SPAD0408
C         RECORDS IN CORE, END OF GROUP SAME AS END OF ITERATION.       SPAD0409
C                                                                       SPAD0410
      IF(NUMBR) 1380,1380,1383                                          SPAD0411
 1380 ASSIGN 120 TO NTP                                                 SPAD0412
      GO TO 1384                                                        SPAD0413
 1383 ASSIGN 9 TO NTP                                                   SPAD0414
 1384 ASSIGN 7 TO IESKP                                                 SPAD0415
C                                                                       SPAD0416
C        IF JWX1 IS -, SPAD IS TO CHECK CONVERGENCE DURING THIS         SPAD0417
C         ITERATION.  SET SWITCH KTST SO THAT A NEW V(I) WILL BE        SPAD0418
C         COMPARED TO THE VALUE COMPUTED BY THE PREVIOUS ITERATION.     SPAD0419
C        OTHERWISE SET KTST TO SKIP THE CONVERGENCE TEST.               SPAD0420
C                                                                       SPAD0421
      IF (JWX1) 1381, 1382,1382                                         SPAD0422
 1381 ASSIGN 127 TO KTST                                                SPAD0423
      GO TO 406                                                         SPAD0424
 1382 ASSIGN 124 TO KTST                                                SPAD0425
C        IF JWX2 IS +, THE POINT RECORDS ARE STORED ON TAPE--WITH       SPAD0426
C         LK GROUPS OF REGULAR INTERIOR POINTS, POSSIBLY PRECEDED       SPAD0427
C         BY A GROUP OF INPUT POINT RECORDS.                            SPAD0428
C                                                                       SPAD0429
 406  IF(JWX2)6,6,300                                                   SPAD0430
C                                                                       SPAD0431
C                                                                       SPAD0432
C        LIMIT IS UPDATED BEFORE COMPUTATION OF V(I) IN EACH GROUP.     SPAD0433
C        LKA  --THE NUMBER OF GROUPS OF REGULAR INTERIOR POINT          SPAD0434
C         RECORDS YET TO BE READ DURING THIS ITERATION.                 SPAD0435
C        INITIALIZE SWITCH  IESKP  TO RETURN TO TAPE READ-IN WHEN       SPAD0436
C         A GROUP IS FINISHED.                                          SPAD0437
C        THE POINT RECORDS HAVE BEEN WRITTEN ON TWO TAPES, NUT1         SPAD0438
C         AND NUT2.  DURING EACH ITERATION, ONE OF THESE TAPES IS       SPAD0439
C         REWOUND, AND POINT RECORDS ARE READ FROM THE OTHER.           SPAD0440
C        FLIP IS THE SWITCH THAT CONTROLS THIS ALTERNATION.             SPAD0441
 300  LIMIT = 0                                                         SPAD0442
      LKA = LK                                                          SPAD0443
      ASSIGN 326 TO IESKP                                               SPAD0444
      IF (FLIP) 224, 324, 224                                           SPAD0445
C                                                                       SPAD0446
C        RESET FLIP TO ALTERNATE VALUE.                                 SPAD0447
C        IF NA4 NON-POSITIVE, THERE ARE NO INPUT POINT RECORDS.         SPAD0448
C         TRANSFER TO READ IN REGULAR INTERIOR POINT RECORDS.           SPAD0449
C        OTHERWISE, READ INPUT POINT RECORDS, SET LIMIT TO NUMBER       SPAD0450
C         OF RECORDS IN THIS GROUP, TRANSFER TO BEGIN COMPUTATION       SPAD0451
C         LOOP OF ITERATION.                                            SPAD0452
C                                                                       SPAD0453
 224  FLIP=0.                                                           SPAD0454
      REWIND  NUT2                                                      SPAD0455
      IF(NA4)326,326,225                                                SPAD0456
 225  READ TAPE  NUT1, (NSTO(I), I = 1, NA4), (ASTO(I), I = 1, NA5)     SPAD0457
      GO TO 339                                                         SPAD0458
C                                                                       SPAD0459
 324  FLIP=1.                                                           SPAD0460
      REWIND  NUT1                                                      SPAD0461
      IF(NA4)326,326,325                                                SPAD0462
 325  READ TAPE  NUT2, (NSTO(I), I = 1, NA4), (ASTO(I), I = 1, NA5)     SPAD0463
 339  LIMIT = NUMBR                                                     SPAD0464
      GO TO 6                                                           SPAD0465
C                                                                       SPAD0466
C        READ IN A GROUP OF REGULAR INTERIOR POINTS FROM TAPE,          SPAD0467
C         AND INITIALIZE FOR COMPUTATION OF V(I) IN THIS GROUP.         SPAD0468
C         (LA AND IHK ARE RELATED TO LOCATION OF POINT RECORDS          SPAD0469
C         IN CORE DURING COMPUTATION.)                                  SPAD0470
C        LIMIT IS UPDATED TO THE END OF THE GROUP TO BE READ IN.        SPAD0471
C                                                                       SPAD0472
 326  IHK = 2                                                           SPAD0473
      LA = 2                                                            SPAD0474
      LIMIT = LIMIT + LPTA                                              SPAD0475
 330  IF(FLIP)328,329,328                                               SPAD0476
C                                                                       SPAD0477
 328  READ TAPE  NUT2, (NSTO(I), I = 1, LT),  (ASTO(I), I = 1, LLT)     SPAD0478
      GO TO 331                                                         SPAD0479
 329  READ TAPE  NUT1, (NSTO(I), I = 1, LT),  (ASTO(I), I = 1, LLT)     SPAD0480
C                                                                       SPAD0481
C        IF LKA=0, THE GROUP JUST READ IN IS THE LAST.  SET IESKP       SPAD0482
C         TO THE END-OF-ITERATION ALTERNATIVE, AND UPDATE LIMIT         SPAD0483
C         TO THE TOTAL NUMBER OF POINT RECORDS.                         SPAD0484
C                                                                       SPAD0485
 331  LKA=LKA-1                                                         SPAD0486
      IF (LKA) 334,334, 6                                               SPAD0487
 334  LIMIT = NPONT                                                     SPAD0488
      ASSIGN 7 TO IESKP                                                 SPAD0489
C                                                                       SPAD0490
C        THERE FOLLOWS THE COMPUTATION LOOP.  V(I) ARE COMPUTED         SPAD0491
C         SUCCESSIVELY UNTIL THE END OF THE GROUP IN CORE IS            SPAD0492
C         REACHED, OR ALL V(I) HAVE BEEN COMPUTED.                      SPAD0493
C                                                                       SPAD0494
C        IHK   --THE DIFFERENCE IN INDEX BETWEEN CORRESPONDING          SPAD0495
C         ENTRIES IN NSTO AND ASTO.(THE FIXED-POINT AND FLOATING-       SPAD0496
C         POINT PORTIONS OF POINT-RECORDS.)                             SPAD0497
C        NLA   --THE NUMBER OF NEIGHBOR POINTS IN THE POINT RECORD      SPAD0498
C         OF THE CURRENT V(I),(THE 2ND ENTRY OF ITS FIXED-POINT         SPAD0499
C         RECORD.                                                       SPAD0500
C        IK3   --THE NUMBER ASSIGNED TO THE V(I) CURRENTLY BEING        SPAD0501
C         COMPUTED,(THE 1ST ENTRY OF ITS FIXED-POINT RECORD.)           SPAD0502
C        IBGN, IEND -- RESPECTIVELY THE FIRST AND LAST POINT            SPAD0503
C          NUMBERS OF NEIGHBOR POINTS IN THE CURRENT FIXED-             SPAD0504
C          POINT RECORD.                                                SPAD0505
C                                                                       SPAD0506
 6    NLA = NSTO(LA)                                                    SPAD0507
      IK3 = NSTO(LA-1)                                                  SPAD0508
      IBGN = LA +1                                                      SPAD0509
      IEND = LA +NLA                                                    SPAD0510
      T1 = 0.                                                           SPAD0511
C        DO 3 COMPUTES THE NEW V(I), EXCEPT FOR THE CONSTANT TERM.      SPAD0512
C        IK2   --POINT NUMBER OF A NEIGHBOR POINT, EXTRACTED FROM       SPAD0513
C         FIXED-POINT RECORD.                                           SPAD0514
C        J     --LOCATION OF CORRESPONDING ENTRY IN FLOATING-POINT      SPAD0515
C         RECORD.                                                       SPAD0516
C        T1    --IN WHICH THE PARTIAL SUM OF (COEFFICIENTS*V(NEIGH-     SPAD0517
C         BOR POINTS)) IS ACCUMULATED.                                  SPAD0518
C                                                                       SPAD0519
      DO 3 I = IBGN, IEND                                               SPAD0520
      IK2 = NSTO(I)                                                     SPAD0521
      J = I -IHK                                                        SPAD0522
 3    T1 = T1 + ASTO(J)*V(IK2)                                          SPAD0523
C                                                                       SPAD0524
C        TACK ON THE CONSTANT TERM.                                     SPAD0525
      T1 = T1 + ASTO(J+1)                                               SPAD0526
      LA = IEND +2                                                      SPAD0527
      IHK = IHK +1                                                      SPAD0528
      NKONT=NKONT+1                                                     SPAD0529
C                                                                       SPAD0530
C        SWITCH  NTP  BRANCHES ON TYPE OF POINT RECORD,GOING TO         SPAD0531
C         9 IF AN INPUT POINT RECORD, TO 120 IF A REGULAR INTERIOR      SPAD0532
C         POINT RECORD.                                                 SPAD0533
C                                                                       SPAD0534
C        IF (NUMBR-NKONT) IS ZERO, ALL V(I) CORRESPONDING TO INPUT      SPAD0535
C         POINT RECORDS HAVE BEEN COMPUTED.  SWITCH NTP IS SET          SPAD0536
C         TO THE REGULAR INTERIOR POINT EXIT.                           SPAD0537
      GO TO NTP, (9, 120)                                               SPAD0538
 9    IF (NUMBR -NKONT) 128,128, 121                                    SPAD0539
 128  ASSIGN 120 TO NTP                                                 SPAD0540
      GO TO 121                                                         SPAD0541
C                                                                       SPAD0542
C        OVERRELAXATION IS APPLIED TO ALL BUT INPUT POINT RECORDS.      SPAD0543
C                                                                       SPAD0544
C        SWITCH  KTST  HAS BEEN SET TO 127 IF CONVERGENCE IS TO BE      SPAD0545
C         TESTED DURING THIS ITERATION, OTHERWISE TO 124.               SPAD0546
C                                                                       SPAD0547
C        A RELATIVE CONVERGENCE TEST AGAINST THE CRITERION EPS.         SPAD0548
C        IF THE TEST IS PASSED, NPR IS REDUCED BY 1.                    SPAD0549
C                                                                       SPAD0550
 120  T1 = OMEGA*T1 -OMEGB*V(IK3)                                       SPAD0551
 121  GO TO KTST, (127, 124)                                            SPAD0552
C                                                                       SPAD0553
 127  IF ( ABSF((V(IK3)-T1)/T1) -EPS) 123,123, 124                      SPAD0554
 123  NPR=NPR-1                                                         SPAD0555
C                                                                       SPAD0556
C        STORE THE NEW V(I).                                            SPAD0557
 124  V(IK3) = T1                                                       SPAD0558
C                                                                       SPAD0559
C        COMPARE NKONT AND LIMIT TO DETERMINE IF THE END OF THE         SPAD0560
C         GROUP NOW IN CORE (OR OF THE ITERATION) HAS BEEN REACHED.     SPAD0561
C                                                                       SPAD0562
C        SWITCH  IESKP  HAS BEEN SET TO 326 ONLY IF TAPES ARE USED      SPAD0563
C         AND THE GROUP JUST FINISHED WAS NOT THE LAST.                 SPAD0564
C                                                                       SPAD0565
      IF (NKONT - LIMIT) 6, 340,340                                     SPAD0566
 340  GO TO IESKP, (7, 326)                                             SPAD0567
C                                                                       SPAD0568
C        END OF THE COMPUTATION LOOP.                                   SPAD0569
C        I3    --THE NUMBER OF THE ITERATION JUST COMPLETED.            SPAD0570
C                                                                       SPAD0571
C                                                                       SPAD0572
C        CONTROL IS TRANSFERRED TO SUBROUTINE CNVRG IF--                SPAD0573
C         1.SENSE SWITCH 3 IS DOWN,   OR                                SPAD0574
C         2.NPR=0, INDICATING THAT THE CONVERGENCE CRITERIA HAS         SPAD0575
C            BEEN SATISFIED BY EVERY ONE OF THE V(I), OR                SPAD0576
C         3. MMX1 (=MX1) MAJOR ITERATIONS HAVE BEEN COMPLETED.          SPAD0577
C        OTHERWISE SENSE SWITCH 5 IS TESTED, TO ENSURE THAT CONTROL     SPAD0578
C         WILL TRANSFER TO CNVRG AT LEAST AT THE END OF EVERY RUN.      SPAD0579
C        SENSE SWITCH 5 IS PROVIDED SO THAT A RUN MAY BE HALTED         SPAD0580
C         AND RESULTS SAVED ON NUT3, IF THE RUN EXCEEDS ITS TIME        SPAD0581
C         ALLOTMENT OR MUST BE INTERRUPTED FOR SOME OTHER REASON.       SPAD0582
 7    I3 = I3 +1                                                        SPAD0583
      MMX1 = MMX1-1                                                     SPAD0584
      IF(JWX1) 149,125,125                                              SPAD0585
 149  IF(MMX1) 125,125,1491                                             SPAD0586
C     AFTER MMX1 ITERATIONS, GO TO CNVRG.  THIS SHOULD BE USED WHEN     SPAD0587
C      JWX1 IS NEGATIVE AND SENSE SWITCHES ARE NOT ALLOWED.             SPAD0588
 1491 IF(SENSE SWITCH 3) 125,150                                        SPAD0589
 150  IF (NPR) 125, 125, 152                                            SPAD0590
 152  IF (SENSE SWITCH 5) 125, 126                                      SPAD0591
C                                                                       SPAD0592
 125  CALL CNVRG( V, N111, I3, JWX1, INCD, NPR, EPS, OMEGA, SAVE,       SPAD0593
     1 X1, X2, MX1, MX2)                                                SPAD0594
C     X1, X2, AND MX2 ARE NOT USED AT PRESENT.                          SPAD0595
C        THE FOLLOWING SHOULD BE INCLUDED IN CNVRG                      SPAD0596
C          1. A TEST OF SENSE SWITCH 5, SO THAT APPROPRIATE ACTION      SPAD0597
C              IS TAKEN IF THE OPERATOR FORCES A HALT.                  SPAD0598
C               (PRINTOUT OF RESULTS, SETTING N111 - IF THE V(I)        SPAD0599
C              ARE TO BE SAVED ON TAPE NUT3)                            SPAD0600
C          2. IF THE CONVERGENCE-CHECKING FEATURE OF SPAD IS TO BE      SPAD0601
C              USED, NPR MUST BE TESTED.                                SPAD0602
C         3. TEST OF SENSE SWITCH 3 AND JWX1.  SPADE TRANSFERS TO       SPAD0603
C             CNVRG AFTER EACH ITERATION IF SSW 3 IS DOWN, OR JWX1=+.   SPAD0604
C                                                                       SPAD0605
C        TEST OF N111--  (DO NOT USE -0 FOR -)                          SPAD0606
C         1. IF -, SAVE AND SENSE SWITCH 5 ARE TESTED, TO DETERMINE     SPAD0607
C             IF THE SOLUTION IS TO BE SAVED. TESTING OR SAVING         SPAD0608
C             COMPLETED, THE PROGRAM RETURNS TO STATEMENT 1             SPAD0609
C             FOR THE NEXT CASE.                                        SPAD0610
C         2. IF 0, ANOTHER ITERATION IS BEGUN.                          SPAD0611
C         3. IF +, (THE SET OF EQUATIONS IS NON-LINEAR) SPAD            SPAD0612
C             PROCEEDS TO GO THROUGH THE WHOLE OPERATION OF SETTING     SPAD0613
C             UP POINT RECORDS AGAIN, SO THAT COEFFICIENTS THAT         SPAD0614
C             ARE FUNCTIONS OF THE V(I) MAY BE RECALCULATED.            SPAD0615
C     FOR THE NON-LINEAR CASE (N11=+1), SPAD ALLOWS THE USER TO         SPAD0616
C      RECALCULATE COEFFICIENTS WHICH ARE FUNCTIONS OF THE V(I) FOR     SPAD0617
C      ALL POINT RECORDS.  TO DO THIS, SPAD RETURNS TO STATEMENT 666    SPAD0618
C      AFTER EACH MAJOR ITERATION.  THUS, THE USER MUST PROVIDE FOR     SPAD0619
C      THIS IN BOTH SETUP AND COCAL.  ALSO, THE USER MUST NOT CLEAR     SPAD0620
C      THE V REGION AFTER THE 1ST PASS THRU SETUP.  IF DATA IS LOADED   SPAD0621
C      FROM TAPE NINPT, THE USER MUST SET NINPT=-14 (OR -K) DURING THE  SPAD0622
C      2ND PASS THRU SETUP TO PREVENT SPAD FROM RE-LOADING THE DATA.    SPAD0623
      MMX1 = MX1                                                        SPAD0624
 126  IF (N111) 499, 138, 666                                           SPAD0625
C                                                                       SPAD0626
C        IF SAVE IS NEGATIVE, OR SENSE SWITCH 5 IS DOWN, THE FINAL      SPAD0627
C         V(I) WILL BE SAVED ON TAPE NUT3.   (DESTROYS NINPT, IF ANY.)  SPAD0628
C                                                                       SPAD0629
 499  IF(SAVE)501,500,500                                               SPAD0630
 500  IF(SENSE SWITCH 5)501,1                                           SPAD0631
 501  REWIND  NUT3                                                      SPAD0632
      WRITE TAPE  NUT3, (V(I), I = 1, KUN)                              SPAD0633
      REWIND  NUT3                                                      SPAD0634
C     KUN SHOULD EQUAL THE DIMENSION OF V.  (OR U)                      SPAD0635
      GO TO 1                                                           SPAD0636
C                                                                       SPAD0637
C     THIS PROGRAM IS BEYOND THE MIND OF MORTAL MAN TO CONTEMPLATE.     SPAD0638
C     LET THE USER BEWARE, AND MAY GOD HAVE MERCY UPON HIS SOUL--       SPAD0639
C     POOR DEVIL.                                                       SPAD0640
C     A J. WOLFGANG VON HOLTSTEINOVITCH MODIFICATION  *****             SPAD0641
      END                                                               SPAD0642
